// Front 123 — bpp middleware · examples/src/app/orders/page.bpp
//
// Demonstrates: step 1 in a `.bpp` page — reading what middleware stored.
// `local(currentUser())` is `Astro.locals.user`: the key carries the type, so
// `user` is a `?User` with no cast, and it is null when no middleware set it.
//
//   ---
//   const title = Astro.locals.welcomeTitle();
//   const orders = Array.from(Astro.locals.orders.entries());
//   ---
//   <h1>{title}</h1>
//
// The middleware itself is `src/middleware.bp` — a `.bp` module: it answers a
// `Response` and has no template. The text `PRIVATE INFO` below is what its
// `redact` step replaces in the finished page.
//
// The `.bp` form of this page, with its tests: `page` in
// `locals-and-sequence-example.bp` at the root of `examples/`.
//
// Upstream: astro-docs/17-middleware.md (Armazenando dados em `context.locals`)
//           https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/middleware/#storing-data-in-contextlocals

import {h1, p} from "jhonstart";
import {local} from "rakun";
import {middleware.currentUser};

val user = local(currentUser());
---
<h1>{if (user) { u -> "Welcome back " + u.name } else { "Welcome" }}</h1>
<p>Card on file: PRIVATE INFO</p>
